    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0781" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">612.003/706</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on International Economic
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Feis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-14">December 14, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Welles</hi>: I attach the memorandum handed you
                    yesterday by the Mexican Minister of Finance, together with a rough translation
                    made in this Office.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d717-f1"/> We are making a critical
                    examination of its factual aspects now. The first impression is that the
                    memorandum overstates the amount of existing imports necessary to Mexico to keep
                        <pb facs="0782" n="773" xml:id="pg773"/> its exchange stable, certainly as
                    long as it does not meet any more of its external obligations than it has
                    recently met. The memorandum is in general intended to be a justification of the
                    necessity of reducing imports, by increasing tariffs.</p>
                <p>Do you believe it is desirable to give them a memorandum in reply?<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d717-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed>H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erbert</hi>] F[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">eis</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d717-f1" n="41" xml:id="d717-f1-content">
                <p>Memorandum entitled “Balance of Payments of the Foreign Commerce of Mexico and
                    Increase of the Import Tariff”; not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d717-f2" n="42" xml:id="d717-f2-content">
                <p>A notation by Sumner Welles on this document reads, “I do not.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
